schema: "0.4"
id: workbench-16-import-export-and-sharing
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns (a CLI learning tool) — Import / Export & Sharing: bundle a deck to a file, import without clobbering, resolve conflicts.
# Theme tenets: warm cream "maker's reference sheet" inside a terminal window; a packing-slip export card + a two-column diff/merge on taped paper; printed labels + handwritten marker titles + mono; 3px cut-paper radius; clay accents.
# Palette: cream #f5f0e8, brown ink #2c2416, marker blue #2980b9, clay orange #e67e22, marker red #e74c3c, marker green #27ae60, sticky yellow #fef3b5, tan #d4c9b5.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    command-line tool's IMPORT / EXPORT & SHARING surface, skinned as a warm cream
    "maker's reference sheet" inside a terminal window — packaging a deck to share
    and safely merging a teammate's bundle. Tactile and hands-on: a packing-slip
    note card, taped diff columns, handwritten conflict marks, printed labels,
    monospace file paths. It is a text-mode tool window, never a web browser page.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a single TERMINAL WINDOW showing the IMPORT /
    EXPORT & SHARING surface of "The Robot Learns", a command-line learning tool.
    The content pane is skinned as a warm cream MAKER'S REFERENCE SHEET — note
    cards, masking tape and pushpins on cream paper, split into an EXPORT half and an
    IMPORT half. Fill the frame with ONE tool window and a thin top title bar; NO web
    browser chrome, no tabs, no address bar.

    TITLE BAR (thin, top): a warm cream bar with three small window dots and, in
    fixed-width type, "learn share · export / import".

    LEFT — EXPORT (a packing slip): a pinned note card titled in marker "export
    bundle", listing the deck contents like a shipping manifest — a handwritten deck
    name "Rust Ownership · 48 cards", printed sub-lines ("12 articles", "3 media"),
    and the output file as a monospace path "rust-ownership.trl-bundle". A small
    stack of tiny FLASHCARD cards peeks out behind it, corners fanned.

    RIGHT — IMPORT (a diff/merge): two TAPED COLUMNS side by side under a marker
    title "resolve conflicts", "local" on the left and "incoming" on the right, a
    strip of masking tape running down the seam between them. Three rows compare
    entries in monospace; one row is clean (a green marker tick), one is a conflict
    (handwritten marker-red marks on both sides) with two small taped toggles
    "keep mine / take theirs", one is a brand-new card (a blue "+ new" mark). A red
    pushpin sits on the conflicting row.

    A hand-drawn arrow curves from the export card toward a small note "publish to
    library (soon)".

    BOTTOM STATUS RULE: a persistent thin bar with fixed-width keybind hints
    "^X export   ^I import   ^Enter resolve   ^Q quit".

    PALETTE & TYPE: warm cream paper with brown-ink text; friendly clay accents —
    marker blue for the primary/new mark, clay orange for tape and accent borders,
    marker red for conflict marks and the pushpin, marker green for the clean tick.
    Handwritten marker script for card titles and conflict marks, a clean printed
    geometric sans for labels, fixed-width monospace for file paths and diff rows.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: barely-rounded cut-paper corners; cards lifted off the sheet by
    soft warm-brown drop shadows; the two diff columns joined by a real strip of
    tape; separation by air, tape and shadow rather than ruled boxes; light paper
    grain that never hurts legibility.

    MOOD: two makers swapping parts across a bench — hands-on, careful, encouraging;
    conflicts handled by hand on warm paper, never a clinical merge tool.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, web browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, marketing web page, sterile flat corporate merge tool, dark terminal background, monochrome CRT"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Reads as an import/export & sharing surface skinned as a maker's cream sheet: an EXPORT packing-slip card listing deck contents + output file path with a fanned flashcard stack, and an IMPORT diff/merge with two taped local-vs-incoming columns, a clean tick row, a conflict row with keep/take toggles, and a new-card row; title bar; bottom keybind status rule"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Warm cream paper + brown ink with clay accents; handwritten marker titles/conflict marks + printed sans labels + monospace paths/diff; pinned cards + taped seam with soft warm shadows; cut-paper radius; light not dark"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear export/import split, legible diff columns, plausible real tool window"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "web browser chrome or a marketing web page instead of a tool window"
    - "dark terminal / monochrome CRT instead of warm cream paper skin"

tags: [workbench, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup]
